// seam rather than imported across it (S2).
//
// The vocabulary is the one a UI already has buttons for. Kirk's ruling on
// rpg-toolkit#1138: "in our ui we hand shapes for action, bonus and reaction
// that lined up with the various things we could do." A client lights the
// shape a declaration names and never learns why that shape is the one.
//
// NONE IS NOT UNSPECIFIED, and the distinction is load-bearing. The SDK spells
// SlotNone as the empty string "", and "this swing spends no shape" is an
// ANSWER: Extra Attack's second swing draws a banked attack and lights none of
// the three shapes, yet it is still priced and can still be unaffordable once
// that bank runs out. Go's zero value for session.Slot is therefore a real
